WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.701
-Donald Trump is reportedly
planning to run

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.767
for president again to as a way
to protect himself

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.534
from a possible criminal
indictment

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:10.400
related to the attempted coup on
January 6th.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.667
Meanwhile, the committee
investigating the coup

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.634
is planning to reveal
new details tomorrow

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:17.200
about what Trump
was doing that day

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.300
as the mob he incited
ransacked the Capitol

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.567
and tried to overturn
the election.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.934
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:27.467
♪♪

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:30.033
At this point, the January 6th
committee hearing

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:32.434
have provided us with ample
evidence that Trump

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:35.901
and his gang of oddly shaped
goons committed multiple crimes.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:38.701
I mean, that seemed
obvious on the day

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.901
the insurrection happened,
but now

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:42.267
we have a lot more detail.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.767
It's kind of like how if you see
an employee at Dairy Queen

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.934
covered in ice cream with his
pants around his ankles.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.267
You might think, "Is Chad
sticking his doink

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:50.868
in the soft serve machine?"

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:53.734
But then when you find a
detailed memo on his laptop

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:56.434
titled "Chad's Six Point Plan
for Dipping Doinks in the

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:59.367
Soft Serve Machine,"
you know for sure.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.634
Even the Justice Department
seems taken aback

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:03.901
by all the new evidence the
committee has accumulated.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:06.901
And as a result, the Feds are
now talking more openly

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:10.167
about Trump's behavior and
whether it constitutes a crime.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.367
-According to
"The New York Times,"

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:13.100
the shocking testimony
of Cassidy Hutchinson

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.067
was so profound that it jolted
top Justice Department

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:18.100
officials into discussing
the topic

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.267
of Mr. Trump more directly,
at times in the presence of

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:23.133
Attorney General
Merrick Garland.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:25.667
-Okay, I mean, I get that
Cassidy Hutchinson's

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.868
testimony was shocking,
but you're just now

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.767
getting around
to discussing Trump?

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.901
You're six years late.

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:36.434
Did you also just start watching
"Fleabag?"

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.367
Cheeky.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:40.133
And Trump apparently
is quite afraid

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.701
of the various criminal
investigations

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.367
into his activities
on January 6th,

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.100
which is reportedly
one of the reasons why

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.934
he's likely to run again
and wants to announce soon.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:51.200
He thinks being a candidate, and
specifically president again

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.067
will protect him
from going to jail.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:54.701
-And now as the Justice
Department debates this,

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.667
he is telling people around him
he's going to run

00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:00.234
for reelection as the ultimate
get-out-jail-free card.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:02.400
-Many people around the
president who I spoke to

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.767
were talking about his concerns
about facing prosecution.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:10.701
He's under investigations in all
sorts of different jurisdictions

00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:12.534
in New York, in New York City,

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:15.000
with Department of Justice
in Georgia.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.634
-He's under investigation
in New York, Washington,

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:20.667
Georgia, Peoria, Mayberry,
Twin Peaks,

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:23.300
Tatooine, Westeros, Xanadu.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.000
He's even under investigation on
the planet from "Avatar"

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.033
for disguising himself as Na'vi
to steal some unobtanium.

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:31.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.400
Incidentally, that's always what
he looked like

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.133
After he took
hydroxychloroquine.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.734
"Rudy, I'm blue."

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:37.901
"Me too, boss.

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:39.767
I just find out
I married my cousin."

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:44.067
And that was today's unnecessary
Rudy reference.

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:45.734
-All the networks!

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:48.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.267
-It's pretty amazing that when
Trump ran in 2016

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:55.200
his slogan was "lock her up,"
and in 2024 it's going to be

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.167
"vote for me
or I'm gonna go to jail."

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:00.501
I, for one, don't think
Trump needs another

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:01.868
get-out-of-jail-free card.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:04.267
His whole life has been a
get-out-of-jail-free card.

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.000
Pretty sure Trump could park
his golf cart

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.334
in the middle of the BQE during
rush hour

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:10.701
and the cops would just set up
orange cones around him.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:14.367
Meanwhile, I park my car
in the fire lane for a minute

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:17.601
just to run into a CVS to see
if they have Clif Bar I like.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.801
And when I get back, there are
nine different tickets plastered

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:22.200
on my window for stuff
like illegal parking,

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.501
blocking a fire lane, impending
an emergency vehicle

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:27.167
and one that just says "having
a big [bleep] mouth,

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.300
you smartass."

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:32.200
So, Trump's plan, apparently,
is to run for president again

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.567
because he thinks that will
protect him from being indicated

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:37.067
by any of the various legal
entities investigating him.

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:40.067
And Trump knows he's
the one on the hot seat,

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:41.834
because to state the obvious,
none of this

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:42.868
would have happened without him.

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:44.267
All the various crimes
documented

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:45.868
by the committee
flow from him.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:47.100
He's the kingpin.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.467
Even if one of his cronies
broke the law

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.901
at his direction, that
implicates him, too.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:54.300
I mean, it's not like these
random dudes just got together

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.200
and hatched a plan
for a coup without him.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.801
It wasn't a surprise
birthday party.

00:03:57.801 --> 00:03:59.167
There wasn't a magician there.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.267
And if there was,
Trump would have tried

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:03.334
to rope the magician
in to the coup, too.

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.334
"Oh, and look, there's a quarter
behind your ear."

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:06.467
"That's fantastic.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:09.033
Now make Mike Pence disappear."

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:11.000
Trump got this gang
of criminal goons

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.634
together himself,
and for the express purpose

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:15.834
of formulating a plan
to overturn the election

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:18.033
and stage a coup,
a plan which, at this point,

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:19.667
has been documented in
painstaking

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.033
detail by the committee.

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:23.033
-Throughout all these hearings,
they have been incredibly

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:27.100
consistent and rigorous about
how the ultimate culpability

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.534
for that dark day
and what led up to it

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.834
rests with Donald Trump.

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:35.033
And about how it was he that
plucked out these seemingly

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.667
random people, from a former
Federal Prosecutor

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:40.067
turned conspiracy
theory promoter, Sydney Powell,

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:43.267
to, well, the right-wing
pillow-selling dude,

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:46.400
to a random underling
in environmental law

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.300
at the Department of Justice,
Jeffrey Clark,

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.667
to another random right-wing
law professor who became

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:53.734
the author of the infamous coup
memo, John Eastman.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:58.300
And he put this crew together to
try to end American democracy.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.434
They didn't all know
each other beforehand.

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:02.601
It was Trump
that got them together.

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.567
It all flows from one man,
Donald Trump.

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.234
-This is the kind of
crew you'd put together

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:10.434
for "Ocean's Eleven"
if the goal was to get caught.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:13.033
"We couldn't find an explosives
expert, but this guy

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:14.534
says he knows pillows."

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:17.534
"Hey, good news, every so often
one of my pillows does

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:19.934
spontaneously combust!"

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:21.968
Although I will say, contrary
to that clip,

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:24.167
I do feel like there
is a chance these four had

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:25.834
already met each other
in advance.

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:28.534
I mean, weirdos
find other weirdos.

00:05:28.534 --> 00:05:31.367
Once normal people don't want
to spend time with you,

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.200
your friend options
are pretty limited.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.801
I mean, remember, Sydney Powell
from her January 6th deposition

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:39.067
last week, repeating insane
conspiracy theories

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:41.334
And chugging diet Dr. Pepper?

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:43.467
-In the short period of time
you had with the president,

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:46.801
did he seem receptive
to the presentation

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:48.100
that you were making?

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:10.133
-Regular people aren't going to
hang out with that lady.

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:13.400
Can you imagine Sydney Powell
just, like, going to a barbecue

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.334
at her neighbor's house,
talking about something

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:17.467
boring like re-seeding
your lawn?

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:20.367
"The reason your lawn is dead
is because Hugo Chavez

00:06:20.367 --> 00:06:23.300
and the CIA teamed up
to turn off your sprinklers

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.968
using Dominion software
and Chinese satellites.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:28.901
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'm going to unhinge my jaw

00:06:28.901 --> 00:06:31.267
and chug this entire can of
Diet Dr. Pepper

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:33.334
in one large gulp."

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:36.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.267 --> 00:06:38.434
That's when the couple hosting
the party goes inside,

00:06:38.434 --> 00:06:39.901
gets into a fight
about whose fault it is

00:06:39.901 --> 00:06:41.567
that she got invited
in the first place.

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.400
"I told you not to invite
your work friends!"

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.467
"I thought I could
set her up with Rudy!"

00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:47.434
"Excuse me, Ms. Powell,
that's a lovely

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:48.567
soft drink you have there.

00:06:48.567 --> 00:06:50.200
Any chance I'm related to you?

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.968
Don't answer, it's spicier
if I'm never sure."

00:06:52.968 --> 00:06:56.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.601
Sorry, guys, we did another one.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.767
-America!

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:02.667
-And by the way,
that gang of weirdos Trump

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:05.167
brought together is still
trying to root out

00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:08.267
nonexistent voter fraud,
even amid all the investigations

00:07:08.267 --> 00:07:09.367
that are currently happening.

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:11.267
Like Mypillow CEO Mike Lindell

00:07:11.267 --> 00:07:12.834
who said last week he's flying

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:15.934
in a plane full
of "cyber guys" to Arizona,

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.334
whatever the hell that means.

00:07:17.334 --> 00:07:19.467
-I'm going to look
at the evidence.

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:23.634
On July 21st, I've got a
planeload of lawyers,

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:27.801
cyber guys, experts,
flying into Arizona.

00:07:27.801 --> 00:07:31.167
We're flying a planeload
of lawyers down there, Brandon,

00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:34.834
experts, cyber guys to testify.

00:07:34.834 --> 00:07:39.133
-"Cyber guys" sounds like what
your dad calls "Transformers."

00:07:39.133 --> 00:07:41.667
"You know, if you ever get tired
Of watching your cyber guys,

00:07:41.667 --> 00:07:44.968
the grass out back
ain't getting any shorter."

00:07:44.968 --> 00:07:47.400
That's right, Mike Lindell,
ol' Mike Lindell claims

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.234
he's flying a plane of
cyber guys down to Arizona

00:07:50.234 --> 00:07:51.868
to prove voter fraud
or something.

00:07:51.868 --> 00:07:53.667
Although, there's a good chance
Mike Lindell thinks

00:07:53.667 --> 00:07:56.667
any commercial airline
is a plane full of cyber guys,

00:07:56.667 --> 00:07:59.300
because all the passengers
are sitting in front of screens.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:02.701
"It's a plane full of tech
wizards and cyber guys

00:08:02.701 --> 00:08:05.200
who've got their own computers
built into the seats

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:08.534
in front of them, and these
computers are so advanced

00:08:08.534 --> 00:08:10.701
you can pull up any
movie you want,

00:08:10.701 --> 00:08:13.400
including "Gone Girl"
or the "Austin Powers" one

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.634
Or that one where
Leonardo DiCaprio

00:08:15.634 --> 00:08:18.667
almost gets eaten by the bear!"

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:21.968
The straightforward, fundamental
question at the heart of these

00:08:21.968 --> 00:08:24.534
Hearings and at the heart of our
politics at the moment

00:08:24.534 --> 00:08:26.067
is whether we're
a nation of laws.

00:08:26.067 --> 00:08:28.501
If Trump can simply
escape accountability

00:08:28.501 --> 00:08:30.801
for a criminal plan
to overthrow the government

00:08:30.801 --> 00:08:33.801
by running for president and
declaring himself untouchable,

00:08:33.801 --> 00:08:37.100
then we no longer have a
functioning justice system.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:40.400
As the January 6th committee has
documented in painstaking

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:43.567
detail, Trump and his cronies
have committed many crimes,

00:08:43.567 --> 00:08:47.033
from inciting a riot
to doing this on camera.

00:08:50.667 --> 00:08:52.400
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:56.200
♪♪

